      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High-glycemic index foods cause a rapid increase in blood sugar due to their quick digestion, which leads to a corresponding spike in insulin levels. In contrast, low-glycemic index foods release sugar more slowly, causing a gradual increase in blood sugar and insulin levels, making them better for long-term stability. Both play significant roles in dietary planning, particularly for those with insulin sensitivity issues.",
